    "media:imagetext": "Safety\nSeguridad\nSi usted se encuentra sentado/a an una fila de asientos a la par de una\nsalida u usted no entiende el idioma ingles, favor de avisarle a un tripulante\nSécurité\nSi vous êtes assis dans une rangée de sièges à côté d'une sortie, et vous ne\ncomprenez pas la langue anglaise, veuillez le dire à un membre de l'équipage\nSicherheit\nWenn Sie in einer Sitzreihe neben einem Ausgang sitzen und Sie\nverstehen kein Englisch, bitte verständigen Sie die Flugzeugbesatzung\nLeistream\nEmergency exits are often heavy, awkward to ift, push, pull, and maneuver\nwhen opening. Because of this, and for the benefit of all passengers, Federal Law\nrequires that we seat only able bodied passengers next to emergency exits.\nIf you are sitting in the row of seats next to an exit, you may be asked to open\nthe exit and assist our crew in the event of an emergency.\nIF YOU ARE SITTING IN AN EXIT ROW, PLEASE ASK TO BE RESEATED IF:\n•You have a physical condition which may not be visible and which may prevent\nyou from assisting our crew.\n•You think you lack the strength, mobility, dexterity, or balance required to open\nthe exit and assist our crew.\n• You do not think you could reach the exit, open it, and get out quickly.\n•You believe the physical exertion required to open the exit would injure you.\n•You are hearing impaired and could not hear verbal commands from our crew.\n•You are not able to give oral commands to other passengers.\n•You do not understand the instructions in this brochure.\n•You have other responsibilities (such as a small child to care for) which would\nprevent you from assisting our crew.\n•You are less than 15 years old.\n•You do not wish to assist our crew in this way.\nFederal law requires that all passengers, regardless of where they are\nsitting or their physical condition, must review this important information.\nFollow these instructions, the directions of the crew, and posted signs.\nPlease do not remove this card from the aircraft.\nIf you are sitting in an exit row and you\ncan not read the small type on this card,\nplease tell a crew member.\nUNITED EXPRESS\n® \"UNITED EXPRESS\" is a service mark of United Airlines, Inc.",
